# L §5.7 Bindings (round 8): a binding whose day is a hole is a hole only where a thing of the kind, known at the
# cut, could be alive on one of its possible days; where none could, it binds nothing ('a binding over adjustments
# before any adjustment exists'). d0 is a stated hole (any day is possible): no adjustment and no pet exists, so adj
# and none_alive count nothing (0, L §5.11: count of no member); ana is alive, so some_alive is the hole. ruled_out:
# ana fails the where (she is no pet) whatever the day, so the domain is decided without the day (L §8.1: a hole
# stops propagating where the outcome is decided without it): 0. no_row: at cut 2026-06-30 d1 has no row
# (HOLE-UNGOVERNED, read with no law date), and no adjustment exists: 0, with no question needed.
=== m.tally
model p17
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind persons
kind pets

input d0: date
input d1: date

ask adj: count(a in adjustments on d0) law 2026-06-30
ask none_alive: count(x in pets on d0) law 2026-06-30
ask some_alive: count(p in persons on d0) law 2026-06-30
ask ruled_out: count(p in persons on d0 where p in pets) law 2026-06-30
ask no_row: count(a in adjustments on d1) as known 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d0 = ?"which day?"
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-01-01..

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-07-01
  d1 = 2026-07-01
=== expect
adj: 0
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
no_row: 0
  cut 2026-06-30
none_alive: 0
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
ruled_out: 0
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
some_alive: ?"which day?" (d0)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-10-18
